course: dictionary
lesson: 2114
title: Convenience: easy and useful
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Convenience means being easy, useful or quick for you, so it saves time or trouble. «For convenience, we eat at school.» The clue is saves time: eating at school means you do not have to go home first, so it is easier.
explain: A convenience can also be a thing that makes life easier, like a microwave. At your convenience means at a time that suits you. Ask yourself: does the sentence say something saves you effort or fits your needs? If yes, convenience is probably the right meaning.
explain: Some words are chosen to be polite. «Public conveniences» on a sign means public toilets, so the sign does not have to use the toilet word. Corner shops are small shops open for long hours, and «you pay for convenience» means you pay extra for being close and open late.
fact: Convenience means being easy, useful or quick for you.
fact: A convenience is a thing that makes life easier, like a microwave.
fact: «At your convenience» means at a time that suits you.
fact: «Public conveniences» is a polite name for public toilets.
fact: A «convenience fee» is an extra charge for paying online or by card (US).
exercise: «For convenience, we eat at school.» What does convenience mean here? | Being a school rule that is never changed | Being a kind of food | *Being easy and quick for you, saving time | Being very expensive
exercise: «You can pay at your convenience.» What does at your convenience mean? | Without paying anything | *At a time that suits you | At the same time as everyone else | Only on Sundays
exercise: A sign says «Public conveniences this way.» What does it mean? | *Public toilets | Places to buy microwaves | Free bus stops | Shops that sell food
test: «Convenience food is quick to prepare, but it is often less healthy.» What is convenience food? | Food that you must cook for hours | Food that is always free | *Ready-made food that is quick to prepare | Food grown on a farm by children
test: «Corner shops often charge more than big supermarkets.» Why? | Because they are closed at weekends | Because they sell only healthy food | Because they are far away from you | *Because they are close and open late, so you pay for convenience
exam: «A convenience fee is an extra charge for paying online or by card.» What is a convenience fee? | A free gift from the shop | A discount for buying in bulk | A card with your name on it | *An extra charge for paying the way the shop chose
